{
  "name": "stt-det (settings STT + transcriptions, operator + builder; seeded config + transcripts assert populated, mic + file-picker + delete drive to boundary only)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "The STT page saves through SettingsSubPage (route='stt', onSave): one shared footer (settings-subpage-footer / settings-subpage-save) and a toast (settings-save-toast-success). The page-local sticky bar and inline saved status are gone.",
    "stt-language-select is a native <select> over STT_LANGUAGES, driven with selectOption. It is set to 'it' before the first save because the save button only enables on a real change, and neither the seed ('en') nor settings-det.json ('de' discarded, 'es' saved) leaves that value, so the dirty state holds whether this script runs standalone or inside master-det.",
    "TranscriptCard no longer anchors the source label (it became the EntityCard title); the card metadata row is asserted on transcript-time + transcript-duration + transcript-text.",
    "Saving hot-reloads the engine: Stt.svelte's onSave sets sttApplied on a successful reloadStt() and only falls back to sttNeedsRestart when the reload throws. The seeded run reloads fine, so the deterministic assertion is stt-applied-notice, not the restart banner.",
    "stt-load-model-btn is played through a stubbed picker: loadModel (SttEssentialSection.svelte:78-102) calls plugin-dialog `open` (the IPC plugin:dialog|open), the stub resolves ${HOME}/.apollia/models/Phi-3-mini-Q4.gguf once, and import_model_file (commands/model_hub.rs:450-506) treats a source already inside the models directory as a no-op (`if dest != source`, both resolved from std::env::home_dir), so no file is copied or truncated. The picked path lands in config.model_path (:95) and dirties the form, which settings-subpage-reset restores from savedBaseline (Stt.svelte:94-96) before the next selectOption.",
    "stt-configure-link sits in the stt-status-banner Card (Transcriptions.svelte:99-153, `{#if $sttStatus}`) and navigates to the STT sub-page (navigateToSettings('stt'), router.ts:25-29); the form is opened without edits so the nav guard never fires.",
    "transcribe-file-error-detail-toggle: handleTranscribeFile (TranscribeFileDialog.svelte:19-28) sets an inline error and RETURNS BEFORE the native picker when $sttStatus exists and model_loaded is false, the state stt-model-not-loaded asserts (Transcriptions.svelte:155). humanize keeps the Error message as detail, so the Disclosure renders and its header composes -toggle (Disclosure.svelte:75). Because stopOnError is false, a `plugin:dialog|open resolve null once` stub is armed right before the click as a safety net (a cancelled picker instead of a hung boot if the guard ever fails) and cleared right after so it cannot swallow a later section's picker. Keep this block out of any recipe that loads a real whisper model.",
    "chat-mic-button is played in chat-det.json, not here: dictation.toggle() (useComposerDictation.svelte.ts:59-77) calls start_tour_recording and stop_tour_recording with no getUserMedia in front, so both IPCs are answered by the harness and the cpal capture is never opened.",
    "The load-model picker is answered with the seed's whisper placeholder (ggml-base.bin), never with an LLM GGUF: measured on d1-stt, picking Phi-3-mini-Q4.gguf reached the saved configuration, the engine started on it, and the app stopped answering after the overlay was created.",
    "stt-test-start and stt-test-stop are played on the settings SttTestCard through the harness: start_tour_recording resolves null (Result<(), String> in commands/stt.rs:976-990, so the real command would open a cpal capture, flow.rs:182-233, and needs an engine the placeholder ggml-base.bin cannot load), which flips recording and swaps the button's testid to stt-test-stop (SttTestCard.svelte:190); stop_tour_recording is rejected with a string, which the catch of toggle (SttTestCard.svelte:128-131) turns into an error toast and a return to stt-test-start, the only scripted end of course since stt-transcribed and stt-dictation-failed are Tauri events no stub can emit (stt-test-result and stt-test-failure stay unreachable). toggle awaits ensureMicPermission first (SttTestCard.svelte:121), a WebView getUserMedia that never throws and whose result is ignored; App.svelte:85-91 already primes it at boot because the seed enables STT, and wry 0.55.1 grants the WebView side (wry_web_view_ui_delegate.rs:126-136), so the click adds no prompt the boot did not already raise."
  ],
